'''''Philodendron hederaceum''''',<ref name="hederaceum">{{GRIN | accessdate=7 July 2010}}</ref>  the '''heartleaf philodendron''' ([[synonym (taxonomy)|syn.]] '''''Philodendron scandens''''') is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Araceae]], [[native plant|native]] to Central America and the Caribbean which is common in the houseplant trade. '''''Philodendron hederaceum'' var. ''hederaceum''''', the "'''velvet philodendron,'''" is a subspecies which is in the houseplant trade under its previous name of ''Philodendron micans''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-11-03 |title=Velvet Leaf Philodendron (Philodendron hederaceum var. hederaceum) |url=https://garden.org/plants/view/226494/Velvet-Leaf-Philodendron-Philodendron-hederaceum-var-hederaceum/ |access-date=2022-11-03 |website=Garden.org |archive-date=2023-10-19 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019114901/https://garden.org/plants/view/226494/Velvet-Leaf-Philodendron-Philodendron-hederaceum-var-hederaceum/ |url-status=live }}</ref> While toxic under certain conditions, it is also under current review for numerous health benefits.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://librarysftp.whitworth.edu:2443/login?url=https://www.proquest.com/scholarly-journals/review-on-philodendron-species-plant-seeking/docview/2237019073 | title = Review on Philodendron Species-Plant Seeking for Validation of its Therapeutic Approaches | date = May 2019 | publisher = Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences and Research | accessdate = 4 October 2023 | archive-date = 21 June 2024 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20240621090245/https://librarysftp.whitworth.edu:2443/login?url=https://www.proquest.com/scholarly-journals/review-on-philodendron-species-plant-seeking/docview/2237019073 | url-status = live }}</ref>

==Etymology==
The name Philodendron originates from the Greek words "Philo", meaning "love", and "dendron", meaning "tree". ''P.&nbsp;hederaceum'' are most comfortable growing in an upwards fashion, usually up the trunk of a tree, hence, the name Philodendron.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 2019 |title=Review on Philodendron Species-Plant Seeking for Validation of its Therapeutic Approaches |url=https://librarysftp.whitworth.edu:2443/login?url=https://www.proquest.com/scholarly-journals/review-on-philodendron-species-plant-seeking/docview/2237019073 |accessdate=4 October 2023 |publisher=Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences and Research |archive-date=21 June 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240621090245/https://librarysftp.whitworth.edu:2443/login?url=https://www.proquest.com/scholarly-journals/review-on-philodendron-species-plant-seeking/docview/2237019073 |url-status=live }}</ref>

